  "faqTitle": "Frequently Asked Questions",
  "faq1Question": "How does bidding work?",
  "faq1Answer": "After you post a delivery request, nearby riders see it and place bids with their own price. You choose which bid to accept — you're never stuck with a price you don't like.",
  "faq2Question": "How do I pay?",
  "faq2Answer": "You pay the rider directly in cash or via bank transfer when your delivery arrives, using the price shown on your tracking screen.",
  "faq3Question": "What is the confirmation code for?",
  "faq3Answer": "It's your proof of delivery. Give the code shown on your tracking screen to the rider only once you've actually received your delivery — this is what lets them mark it complete.",
  "faq4Question": "Can I cancel my request?",
  "faq4Answer": "Yes, anytime before the rider has picked up your package. Once it's been picked up, use \"Report a Problem\" instead if something goes wrong.",
  "faq5Question": "What if my rider cancels?",
  "faq5Answer": "Your request automatically reopens for new bids — you won't need to start over from scratch.",
  "faq6Question": "What does the estimated purchase amount mean?",
  "faq6Answer": "If you need the rider to buy something on your behalf (like picking up food from a restaurant), this tells them roughly how much cash to bring so they can pay for it before bidding.",

